========================================================================
0. BASELINE SANITY — can assumed rates reproduce E1's per-request cost?
========================================================================
implied avg request cost: codex $0.0298 | harness $0.0314
  28k in (85% cached) + 2k out -> $0.0260
  32k in (90% cached) + 2k out -> $0.0273
  -> bracketed around the $0.0314 implied average. rates OK as labels.

========================================================================
1. E1 DECOMPOSITION — cost ratio vs request-count ratio
========================================================================
cost ratio      : 2.81x
request ratio   : 2.67x
per-request     : 1.05x (the rest is token mix/cache, not request count)
=> ~62% of the 16 requests are 'overhead' vs codex's 6.

========================================================================
2. E2 PREFIX PIN — steady-state per-request churn after the swap
========================================================================
region R=  113 tok: $0.000162/req (= R x (1.25-0.10) x P_IN)  ->  per 100 requests: $0.0162
region R=  500 tok: $0.000719/req (= R x (1.25-0.10) x P_IN)  ->  per 100 requests: $0.0719
region R= 1004 tok: $0.001443/req (= R x (1.25-0.10) x P_IN)  ->  per 100 requests: $0.1443
one-time re-write of the 10k pinned prefix at the swap: $0.0148
(region R grows with session length: 113->1004 tok is a 9x multiplier)

========================================================================
3. CHANGE #1 — turn consolidation: 16 -> 8 requests
========================================================================
  16 -> 8 req: ~$0.251 saved on the E1 task (50% of harness cost)
  16 -> 6 req: ~$0.314 saved on the E1 task (62% of harness cost)
  (each eliminated request saves its full average cost: prefix read +
   fresh write + output; overhead requests are pure loss — no work done)

========================================================================
4. CHANGE #3 — codex-family tool surface: 30 -> 12 tools
========================================================================
  30->12 tools x 250 tok = 4500 tok/req prefix:
    per 16-req session: $0.0155 saved; per 100-req session: $0.0627
  30->10 tools x 300 tok = 6000 tok/req prefix:
    per 16-req session: $0.0206 saved; per 100-req session: $0.0836
  (secondary: smaller prefix delays compaction; each avoided compaction
   saves its prefire+compact+continue request burst)

========================================================================
5. CHANGE #1b — MCP discovery: 2 model calls per tool
========================================================================
  1 MCP tool(s) discovered lazily: 2 req x $0.0314 = $0.063
  2 MCP tool(s) discovered lazily: 4 req x $0.0314 = $0.126
  4 MCP tool(s) discovered lazily: 8 req x $0.0314 = $0.251
  in-budget pre-exposure (<=2k tok of MCP schemas) costs one extra cache
  write of 2k tok = $0.0031 once, vs $0.0628 per tool in requests

========================================================================
6. CHANGE #5 — E5 replay bloat: parallel calls -> reasoning siblings
========================================================================
  K=1 siblings x 500 tok, replayed on 10 later requests: $0.0006
  K=5 siblings x 500 tok, replayed on 10 later requests: $0.0031
  explicit parallel_tool_calls=false pins K=1 (codex parity)

========================================================================
7. CHANGE #4 — E6 brick: catastrophic tail (claude messages wire)
========================================================================
  session bricks at 40k ctx: full restart re-pays cold write $0.0625 + all output already generated is stranded
  session bricks at 100k ctx: full restart re-pays cold write $0.1562 + all output already generated is stranded
  (frequency-limited to claude+high-reasoning, but EV = freq x total session cost)
